---
// Englische Fassung der Datenschutzerklärung.
//
// Pfad bleibt /en/datenschutz/ statt /en/privacy/ — siehe Begründung in
// en/impressum.astro: hreflang und Sprachumschalter leiten den deutschen
// Pfad mechanisch ab, ein abweichender Slug zeigte auf eine Seite, die es
// nicht gibt.
//
// Art. 12 DSGVO verlangt eine für die betroffene Person verständliche Form;
// eine englische Fassung ist dafür sinnvoll. Verbindlich bleibt die deutsche.
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy under the GDPR."
>
  <Section
    as="h1"
    width="narrow"
    headerLayout="stacked" title="Privacy policy" eyebrow="Legal">
          <p class="u-measure mb-12 border-l-2 border-ink-300 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-500">
        This is a courtesy translation. The legally binding version is the German
        one at <a href="/datenschutz/" class="text-brand-700 underline">felix-paul.de/datenschutz/</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="prose-content">
        <h2>1. Controller</h2>
        <p>
          The controller for data processing on this website (felix-paul.de) within
          the meaning of the GDPR is:
        </p>
        <p>
          {SITE.author}<br />
          {SITE.street} {SITE.houseNumber}<br />
          {SITE.plz} {SITE.city}, Germany<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        </p>

        <h2>2. Visiting the site (server logs)</h2>
        <p>
          This website is served as static files through Cloudflare Pages. When you
          visit it, technically necessary data (IP address, user agent, referrer,
          timestamp) is processed by Cloudflare in order to deliver the site and keep
          it secure. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in
          secure operation). No further analysis takes place.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Contact form and email</h2>
        <p>
          If you use the contact form or write to me by email, the data you send
          (name, email address, the content of your message and any further details)
          is stored in order to handle your enquiry and to prepare possible
          collaboration. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR (steps prior to a
          contract) or Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR (consent).
        </p>
        <p>
          The contact form currently runs through the service provider
          <strong>FormSubmit</strong>. The data you enter is transmitted to FormSubmit
          for this purpose and forwarded to me by email. Once a backend service of my
          own is in place, FormSubmit will be replaced and this policy updated
          accordingly.
        </p>
        <p>
          The data is deleted once your enquiry has been dealt with, unless statutory
          retention obligations require otherwise.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Retention period</h2>
        <p>
          Personal data is stored only for as long as it is needed for the respective
          purpose, or for as long as statutory retention obligations apply (for
          example under commercial or tax law).
        </p>

        <h2>5. Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted by <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.,
          101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). Cloudflare processes the
          server log data described under point 2. Further information:
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Embedded content and external links</h2>
        <p>
          This website embeds videos from <strong>YouTube</strong> (Google Ireland Ltd.)
          and contains links to external platforms such as <strong>LinkedIn</strong> and
          <strong>GitHub</strong>, as well as to <strong>felix-paul.de</strong> and
          <strong>d-solve.de</strong>. As soon as you play an embedded video or follow
          such a link, the privacy policy of the respective provider applies. YouTube
          videos are loaded in privacy-enhanced mode where technically available.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You have the following rights towards the controller regarding your personal
          data:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
          <li>Right to withdraw consent already given (Art. 7 (3) GDPR)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
          authority about the processing of your personal data. The competent authority
          for my place of business is:
        </p>
        <p>
          {/* Amtlicher Name der Behörde — wird nicht übersetzt, aber als
              deutsch ausgezeichnet, damit Screenreader ihn richtig sprechen. */}
          <span lang="de">Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Rheinland-Pfalz</span><br />
          Hintere Bleiche 34, 55116 Mainz, Germany<br />
          <a href="https://www.datenschutz.rlp.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">datenschutz.rlp.de</a>
        </p>

        <h2>9. No tracking cookies, no analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This website sets no tracking cookies and uses no third-party analytics
          (no Google Analytics, no Facebook pixel, and nothing comparable).
        </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
